window.SEARCH_INDEX = [{"url": "apply.html", "title": "Apply for a passport or renew one", "description": "How to apply for a new Indian passport, or renew or re-issue one, for an adult or a child: what you need, the steps, how long it takes and what it costs.", "headings": ["Contents", "How long it takes", "Before you start", "Apply online", "The main steps", "Register on Passport Seva", "Fill in the application form", "Pay and book an appointment", "Go to your appointment", "Police verification", "Receive your passport", "Renew or re-issue a passport", "Passports for children", "Lost, stolen or damaged passports", "Other ways to apply", "On your phone", "From outside India", "With help", "Related content", "Take to your appointment"], "text": "Apply for a passport or renew one Use this service to apply for a new Indian passport, or to renew or re-issue one, for an adult or a child. You can also use it to change the details in your passport or replace one that has been lost, stolen or damaged. Your current passport stays valid until its expiry date. You do not need to replace it when ePassports become available at your Passport Office. Contents How long it takes Before you start Apply online The main steps Renew or re-issue a passport Passports for children Lost, stolen or damaged passports Other ways to apply How long it takes Most applications need police verification before the passport is issued. How long that takes depends on your local police station. If you need a passport urgently, apply under the Tatkaal scheme . Once a Tatkaal application is granted, the passport is usually dispatched on the third working day, not counting the day you applied. ! Warning: Do not book travel until you have a valid passport. A re-issued passport has a new number. Before you start You will need: proof of your present address and date of birth a debit or credit card, net banking or UPI to pay the fee online a mobile number and email address your old passport, if you are renewing or re-issuing one You do not need to provide a photo. Your photo and fingerprints are taken at your appointment. The fee you pay is valid for one year. It cannot be moved to a different application. Apply online Start now {{icon:arrow-right:22}} You will go to the official Passport Seva website to register. Already registered? Sign in{{ext}} The main steps {{icon:clock:18}} About 20 minutes online, then one visit to a Passport Seva Kendra. Register on Passport Seva Create an account and choose the Passport Office for your present address. Find your Passport Office . Fill in the application form Choose Fresh for your first passport or Re-issue if you have had one before. Your details must match your documents exactly. You will be asked for every address you have lived at in the last year, for police verification. Pay and book an appointment Pay online by card, net banking, UPI or SBI wallet, then choose an appointment at a Passport Seva Kendra (PSK) or Post Office Passport Seva Kendra (POPSK). You can reschedule twice within a year of your first appointment. Tatkaal appointments can be rescheduled once. Go to your appointment Bring your original documents and one set of self-attested photocopies. Your photo and fingerprints will be taken. You do not need to print your appointment receipt. The confirmation SMS is enough. Police verification The police check the details you gave. This usually happens before your passport is issued. How police verification works . Receive your passport Your passport is sent to you by Speed Post. Track your application to see where it has reached. Renew or re-issue a passport Apply for a re-issue if: your passport has expired or will expire soon the visa pages are full your name, address or other details have changed you want the Emigration Check Required (ECR) status removed it has been lost, stolen or damaged (see below) A re-issue costs the same as a new passport: ₹2,500 for 36 pages or ₹3,500 for 60 pages. Check the fee for your situation . Take your old passport to your appointment. It will be cancelled and returned to you. If you have changed your name after marriage or divorce To add your spouse’s name or change your surname, bring your marriage certificate, or a joint photo declaration signed by both of you (Annexure J). To remove a spouse’s name, bring the divorce decree. To change it, also bring the remarriage certificate or Annexure J. Passports for children A passport for a child under 18 is valid for 5 years, or until they turn 18 if that is sooner. It has 36 pages and costs ₹1,750. Children aged 15 to 17 can choose a 10-year passport instead, at the adult fee. Both parents are assumed to consent unless the form says otherwise. Proof of address can be in a parent"}, {"url": "documents.html", "title": "Documents you need for a passport", "description": "The documents to take to your Passport Seva Kendra appointment: proof of present address, proof of date of birth, Non-ECR proof, and extra documents for children, Tatkaal and government employees.", "headings": ["Your appointment checklist", "Related content"], "text": "Documents you need for a passport Bring the original of each document, and one set of self-attested photocopies, to your appointment. Most adults need one proof of present address and one proof of date of birth. Some people need extra documents. {{icon:info:32}} Your Passport Office may ask for other documents. Check its page on the list of Passport Offices before your appointment. Show all sections Proof of present address – bring one {{icon:chevron-down:18}} Aadhaar card Electors Photo Identity Card (EPIC) water, electricity, telephone (landline or post-paid mobile) or gas connection bill income tax assessment order registered rent agreement passbook of a running bank account with a scheduled public sector, private sector or regional rural bank, with your photo certificate from your employer on letterhead, if it is a reputed company your spouse’s passport, if it names you as spouse and shows your present address a parent’s passport, for children Proof of date of birth – bring one {{icon:chevron-down:18}} If you were born on or after 1 October 2023 , you must use your birth certificate. If you were born before 1 October 2023, you can use: a birth certificate from the Registrar of Births and Deaths or the Municipal Corporation a transfer, school leaving or matriculation certificate showing your date of birth PAN card driving licence Electors Photo Identity Card (EPIC) a Life Insurance Corporation or public company policy bond an extract of your service record or pension payment order, if you work or worked for the government A PAN card, driving licence, EPIC or service record is only accepted if it shows your exact date of birth. Non-ECR proof – if it applies to you {{icon:chevron-down:18}} Emigration Check Required (ECR) status means you need clearance to work in some countries. You can get Non-ECR status if, for example, you have passed Class 10 or higher. Bring proof of the category you belong to, such as your Class 10 certificate. See all Non-ECR categories and documents{{ext}} . Extra documents for children {{icon:chevron-down:18}} a parent’s proof of address can be used parents’ passports, originals and self-attested copies, if they have them Annexure D, signed by both parents, to avoid police verification when a parent has a valid passport Parents can attest their child’s documents. Extra documents for Tatkaal {{icon:chevron-down:18}} Adults need any 3, and under 18s any 2, documents from the Tatkaal list, plus a signed Tatkaal undertaking. See the Tatkaal document list . If your name has changed after marriage or divorce {{icon:chevron-down:18}} to add a spouse’s name: marriage certificate or Annexure J (joint photo declaration) to remove a spouse’s name: divorce decree to change a spouse’s name: divorce decree or death certificate, plus remarriage certificate or Annexure J If you are changing your whole name, follow the standard name change process. If you work for the government, a PSU or a statutory body {{icon:chevron-down:18}} Bring one of these from your employer. It decides when police verification happens: Identity Certificate (Annexure A): no police verification No Objection Certificate (Annexure G): police verification after your passport is issued Prior Intimation Letter (Annexure H): police verification before your passport is issued Dependent family members can also use an Identity Certificate (Annexure A). Your appointment checklist Tick each item as you put it in your folder. Your ticks are saved on this device. Appointment confirmation SMS on your phone Original proof of present address Original proof of date of birth One set of self-attested photocopies of every document Your old passport, if you are re-issuing one Non-ECR proof, if it applies to you Any annexures that apply, signed Tatkaal only: 3 extra documents and the signed undertaking Lost or stolen passport only: a copy of the police report {{icon:printer:20}} Print this checklist Clear ticks Related content Apply for a passport or renew one Tat"}, {"url": "fees.html", "title": "Passport fees", "description": "Indian passport fees from 1 July 2026, with a calculator to work out what you will pay for a new, re-issued or replacement passport, Tatkaal or a Police Clearance Certificate.", "headings": ["Important", "Work out your fee", "You will pay", "All passport fees", "Discount for young children and senior citizens", "How to pay", "Related content"], "text": "Passport fees Passport fees changed on 1 July 2026. You pay online when you book your appointment. Important An adult’s 36-page passport now costs ₹2,500, up from ₹1,500. A 60-page passport now costs ₹3,500, and Tatkaal adds ₹2,500 to any passport fee. Work out your fee Answer the questions to see what you will pay. What do you need? A passport for the first time Renew or re-issue a passport It has expired, is expiring, or the pages are full Change my details or remove ECR status Replace a lost, stolen or damaged passport or Police Clearance Certificate (PCC) How old is the applicant? 8 or under 9 to 14 15 to 17 18 to 60 Over 60 Which passport does the applicant want? Applicants aged 15 to 17 can choose a full 10-year passport. 5 years, or until they turn 18 10 years How many pages? Choose 60 pages if you travel often and need room for visas. 36 pages 60 pages Normal or Tatkaal? Tatkaal is faster and costs ₹2,500 more. Normal Tatkaal You will pay Card payments may have a bank charge of about 1.5% plus tax. SBI net banking has no extra charge. Start again All passport fees The Tatkaal fee is added to the passport fee. Fees cannot be refunded. Passport and certificate fees from 1 July 2026 Service Fee Extra for Tatkaal New or re-issued passport, 36 pages, 10 years ₹2,500 ₹2,500 New or re-issued passport, 60 pages, 10 years ₹3,500 ₹2,500 New or re-issued passport for under 18s, 36 pages, 5 years or until 18 ₹1,750 ₹2,500 Replacing a lost, stolen or damaged passport, 36 pages, 5 years ₹4,250 ₹2,500 Replacing a lost, stolen or damaged passport, 36 pages, 10 years ₹5,000 ₹2,500 Replacing a lost, stolen or damaged passport, 60 pages ₹6,000 ₹2,500 Changing details or removing ECR, 36 pages, 10 years ₹2,500 ₹2,500 Changing details or removing ECR, 60 pages, 10 years ₹3,500 ₹2,500 Changing details or removing ECR for under 18s, 36 pages ₹1,750 ₹2,500 Police Clearance Certificate (PCC) ₹750 Not available Global Entry Program background verification ₹750 Not available Changing details or removing ECR gets you a new passport booklet. Discount for young children and senior citizens For a new passport (not a re-issue), you get 10% off the basic passport fee if the applicant is 8 or under, or over 60. There is no fee for diplomatic or official passports. How to pay You must pay online before you can book an appointment. You can pay by: debit or credit card (Visa, Mastercard or RuPay) net banking (SBI and other banks) UPI SBI wallet Your payment is valid for one year from the date you paid, or from your first appointment if you have booked one. It cannot be moved to another application. If money left your account but the payment shows as failed or pending If the status is Pending , check again on the next working day using Track Payment Status on your Applicant Home page. If the status is Failed , SBI will refund your bank within 7 working days. If it does not, email customercare.00691@sbi.co.in or call 011-41561114 (10am to 5pm) with your application reference number, transaction ID, amount and date. If you paid twice, the Regional Passport Office will refund the extra payment. Related content Apply for a passport or renew one Get a passport urgently (Tatkaal) Documents you need Official fee structure{{ext}}"}, {"url": "help.html", "title": "Help and frequently asked questions", "description": "Contact the National Call Centre, get answers about appointments, payments and police verification, learn about ePassports, and read the accessibility statement.", "headings": ["Contents", "Contact us", "National Call Centre", "Complaints and feedback", "Payment problems", "Information requests", "Appointments and payments", "How police verification works", "If your police report is adverse", "If police verification is taking a long time", "ePassports", "Accessibility statement", "Known issues", "Report a problem", "Related content"], "text": "Help and frequently asked questions Answers to common questions about passport appointments, payments and police verification. Contents Contact us Appointments and payments How police verification works ePassports Accessibility statement Contact us National Call Centre {{icon:phone:24}} 1800-258-1800 (toll free) For questions about applications, appointments, fees and the status of your passport. Complaints and feedback Register a grievance or give feedback{{ext}} . You will get a reference number to track it. Payment problems Email the SBI helpdesk at customercare.00691@sbi.co.in or call 011-41561114 , 10am to 5pm. Information requests Use Right to Information (RTI){{ext}} to ask for information held by the Passport Seva Programme. Appointments and payments Show all sections Can I change my appointment? {{icon:chevron-down:18}} Yes. You can reschedule a normal appointment twice within a year of your first appointment date. A Tatkaal appointment can be rescheduled once. A Police Clearance Certificate appointment cannot be rescheduled. Do I need to print my appointment receipt? {{icon:chevron-down:18}} No. The SMS with your appointment details is accepted as proof of your appointment. How long is my payment valid? {{icon:chevron-down:18}} One year from the date you paid. If you have booked an appointment, it is one year from your first appointment date. A payment cannot be moved from one application to another. I paid but could not book an appointment {{icon:chevron-down:18}} Sign in and use Schedule Appointment . You can check your payment with Track Payment Status . Money left my account but the payment failed {{icon:chevron-down:18}} SBI refunds failed payments to your bank within 7 working days. If you have not received it after that, contact the SBI helpdesk with your application reference number, transaction ID, amount and date. Do I need an SBI account to pay? {{icon:chevron-down:18}} No. You can pay with a card or UPI from any bank, or with net banking from SBI and other banks. How police verification works Police verification checks that the details in your application are correct, so a passport does not reach the wrong person. Your Passport Office decides which type you need: Before your passport is issued Most new and re-issue applications After your passport is issued Tatkaal applications, and government employees with a No Objection Certificate (Annexure G) Not needed Usually children whose parent has a valid passport and whose parents both consent (Annexure D), and government employees with an Identity Certificate (Annexure A) You only need proof of your present address. But you must list every address you have lived at in the last year, so the police can check them. If you are from Jammu and Kashmir and live elsewhere, police verification is done at both your present and permanent addresses. If your police report is adverse Contact your Passport Office to find out why. Once the issue is cleared up, you can ask for police verification to be done again. If police verification is taking a long time If you have not received your passport, visit your Passport Office . ePassports An ePassport is a paper passport with an electronic chip inside. The chip holds your personal details and biometric information, digitally signed so border officials anywhere can check it is genuine. You can recognise an ePassport by a small gold symbol on the front cover. You do not need to replace your current passport. It stays valid until it expires. When your Passport Office starts issuing ePassports, new passports from that office will be ePassports. Accessibility statement This prototype is designed to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA and the Guidelines for Indian Government Websites (GIGW) 3.0. You should be able to: make text larger with the A+ button at the top of every page, or zoom up to 400% without content overlapping switch to a high contrast colour scheme use the whole website with a keyboard"}, {"url": "index.html", "title": "Passport Seva", "description": "Apply for an Indian passport, renew or re-issue one, get one urgently under Tatkaal, check fees and documents, and track your application.", "headings": ["Only apply on the official website", "What do you want to do?", "Get a passport", "Certificates and other services", "Before you apply", "Passports and services delivered in 2025", "Notices and updates", "Get help", "mPassport Seva app"], "text": "Indian passports and travel documents Apply for a new passport, renew one, get one urgently, or check where your application has reached. Where are you applying from? India | Outside India{{ext}} {{icon:alert-circle:32}} Only apply on the official website Fake websites such as indiapassport.org and passport-seva.in collect personal data and charge extra fees. The only official websites are passportindia.gov.in and the mPassport Seva app. Government fees are paid online only, and nobody needs to fill in your form for you. What do you want to do? {{icon:passport:32:task-card__icon}} Apply for or renew a passport First passport, renewal or re-issue, for adults and children. {{icon:clock:32:task-card__icon}} Get a passport urgently Tatkaal is processed faster and costs ₹2,500 more. {{icon:route:32:task-card__icon}} Track your application See where your passport has reached using your file number. {{icon:calendar:32:task-card__icon}} Check appointment availability{{ext}} Find the next free slot at a Passport Seva Kendra near you. Get a passport Apply for a new adult passport Who can apply, the steps, documents and photos. Renew or re-issue your passport If it is expiring, full, or your details have changed. Get a passport for your child Applicants under 18, parental consent and validity. Get a passport urgently (Tatkaal) Eligibility, extra documents and how fast it is. Replace a lost, stolen or damaged passport What to report, the fee and the documents to bring. Diplomatic or official passport{{ext}} For eligible government officials travelling on duty. Certificates and other services Police Clearance Certificate (PCC){{ext}} Often needed for work, study or residence abroad. Fee ₹750. Identity Certificate{{ext}} A travel document for people who cannot get a passport. Surrender Certificate{{ext}} If you have taken up the citizenship of another country. Line of Control (LoC) permit{{ext}} For travel across the LoC in Jammu and Kashmir. Global Entry Program verification{{ext}} Background check for the US Global Entry Program. Fee ₹750. Apply from outside India{{ext}} Passport services at Indian embassies and consulates. Before you apply Fees and fee calculator Work out exactly what you will pay. Fees changed in July 2026. Documents you need Proof of address and date of birth, with a printable checklist. Find a Passport Office 37 Regional Passport Offices and 500+ service locations. How police verification works When it happens, and how it affects how long you wait. ePassports The new chip-enabled passport and what it means for you. Help and FAQs Payments, appointments, rescheduling and grievances. Passports and services delivered in 2025 1,40,43,475 in India 18,93,055 at Indian missions abroad 1,59,36,530 in total Notices and updates New Fees Passport fees revised from 1 July 2026 A 36-page passport now costs ₹2,500 and a 60-page passport ₹3,500. Tatkaal adds ₹2,500 to any passport fee. Tatkaal Check you are eligible before applying under Tatkaal Some applicants cannot use the scheme, and you must bring a signed undertaking to your appointment. Appointments Normal and Tatkaal appointment opening times (PDF) {{ext}} When new appointment slots open at each Passport Office. Advisory Going abroad for work? Go safe, go trained (PDF) {{ext}} Advice for Indian citizens taking up a job in another country. ePassport ePassports are being rolled out across Passport Offices Your current passport stays valid until it expires. You do not need to replace it. Get help The National Call Centre answers questions about applications, appointments and payments. {{icon:phone:24}} 1800-258-1800 Help and frequently asked questions Register a grievance or give feedback{{ext}} Right to Information (RTI){{ext}} mPassport Seva app Apply, pay, book appointments and track your application on your phone. Available for Android and iPhone. {{icon:smartphone:18}} Get the app"}, {"url": "offices.html", "title": "Find a Passport Office", "description": "Search India's 37 Regional Passport Offices by city or state, and find out how Passport Offices, Passport Seva Kendras and Post Office Passport Seva Kendras differ.", "headings": ["Types of office", "Regional Passport Offices"], "text": "Find a Passport Office There are 37 Regional Passport Offices in India, and more than 500 places where you can have your appointment. Your Passport Office depends on your present address. It is chosen for you when you register on Passport Seva. Types of office Regional Passport Office (RPO) Checks and grants applications for its area. Visit if you are asked to, for example about a pending or held application. Passport Seva Kendra (PSK) Where most people go for their appointment. Your documents are checked and your photo and fingerprints are taken. Post Office Passport Seva Kendra (POPSK) A Passport Seva Kendra at a head post office, so you can have your appointment closer to home. Find a Passport Seva Kendra or Post Office Passport Seva Kendra near you{{ext}} Regional Passport Offices Search by city or state For example, Kochi or Tamil Nadu Ahmedabad Gujarat Amritsar Punjab Bareilly Uttar Pradesh Bengaluru Karnataka Bhopal Madhya Pradesh Bhubaneswar Odisha Chandigarh Chandigarh Chennai Tamil Nadu Cochin Kerala Coimbatore Tamil Nadu Dehradun Uttarakhand Delhi Delhi Ghaziabad Uttar Pradesh Goa Goa Guwahati Assam Hyderabad Telangana Jaipur Rajasthan Jalandhar Punjab Jammu Jammu and Kashmir Kolkata West Bengal Kota Rajasthan Kozhikode Kerala Lucknow Uttar Pradesh Madurai Tamil Nadu Mumbai Maharashtra Nagpur Maharashtra Patna Bihar Pune Maharashtra Raipur Chhattisgarh Ranchi Jharkhand Shimla Himachal Pradesh Srinagar Jammu and Kashmir Surat Gujarat Tiruchirappalli Tamil Nadu Trivandrum Kerala Vijayawada Andhra Pradesh Visakhapatnam Andhra Pradesh No Passport Office matches your search. Check the spelling, or search for your state instead. Each Passport Office may ask for extra documents. Check your office’s page on the official list of Passport Offices{{ext}} ."}, {"url": "tatkaal.html", "title": "Get a passport urgently (Tatkaal)", "description": "The Tatkaal scheme is a faster way to get a new or re-issued Indian passport. Check if you are eligible, the extra documents you need and what it costs.", "headings": ["How Tatkaal works", "Documents you need", "Sign the Tatkaal undertaking", "Who cannot apply under Tatkaal", "Tatkaal fees", "Apply", "Related content"], "text": "Passports Get a passport urgently (Tatkaal) Tatkaal is a faster service for new and re-issued passports. It costs ₹2,500 on top of the normal passport fee. Total fee from ₹5,000 for an adult’s 36-page passport When your passport is sent usually the 3rd working day after it is granted Police verification after your passport is issued Rescheduling once, within a year of your first appointment How Tatkaal works Tatkaal applications are processed faster and printed in a separate queue. Police verification happens after the passport is issued, not before. When you book, you can choose a Tatkaal or a Normal appointment slot. If no Tatkaal slot suits you, you can take a Normal slot. You still pay the Tatkaal fee, and your application is still processed under Tatkaal. Your passport office makes the final decision on whether to issue a passport under Tatkaal. Documents you need You do not need a verification certificate from a Gazetted Officer. Instead, bring originals of: any 3 documents from the list below if you are 18 or over any 2 documents from the list if you are under 18 Also bring the usual proof of address and date of birth , and Non-ECR proof if it applies to you. Documents accepted for Tatkaal Aadhaar card or e-Aadhaar Electors Photo Identity Card (EPIC) Service photo identity card from a State or Central Government body, PSU, local body or public limited company Scheduled Caste, Scheduled Tribe or Other Backward Class certificate Arms licence Pension document, such as an ex-serviceman’s pension book or pension payment order Your last passport (re-issue only) PAN card Bank, Kisan or Post Office passbook Student photo identity card from a recognised educational institution Driving licence from the state where you are applying Birth certificate Ration card Sign the Tatkaal undertaking Download, fill in and sign the undertaking, then bring it to your appointment. Undertaking for Tatkaal scheme – English (PDF){{ext}} Undertaking for Tatkaal scheme – Hindi (PDF){{ext}} ! Warning: If any Tatkaal document is missing or not in order, your application will be put on hold. It will be closed if the documents are not provided within 90 days. Who cannot apply under Tatkaal Some applicants cannot use Tatkaal. Check the list before you pay: Categories not eligible for Tatkaal – English (PDF){{ext}} Categories not eligible for Tatkaal – Hindi (PDF){{ext}} For example, you cannot use Tatkaal if you live in Nagaland, or if your passport is damaged so badly that the number, name or photo cannot be read. Tatkaal fees Total Tatkaal fee by type of passport Passport Passport fee Tatkaal fee Total Adult, 36 pages, new or re-issue ₹2,500 ₹2,500 ₹5,000 Adult, 60 pages, new or re-issue ₹3,500 ₹2,500 ₹6,000 Under 18, 36 pages, new or re-issue ₹1,750 ₹2,500 ₹4,250 Replacing a lost, stolen or damaged passport, 36 pages ₹5,000 ₹2,500 ₹7,500 Replacing a lost, stolen or damaged passport, 60 pages ₹6,000 ₹2,500 ₹8,500 You pay the full Tatkaal amount online when you book. Use the fee calculator to check your exact fee. Apply Register or sign in on the official website, choose Tatkaal as the scheme on the form, then pay and book. Start now {{icon:arrow-right:22}} Related content Apply for a passport or renew one Passport fees Documents you need Appointment opening times (PDF){{ext}} Track your application"}, {"url": "track.html", "title": "Track your passport application", "description": "Check where your passport application has reached using your file number and date of birth, and find out what each status means.", "headings": ["There is a problem", "Your details are ready to check", "What your status means", "If your application is on hold", "If your police report is adverse", "If you have waited a long time", "Other ways to track", "Related content"], "text": "There is a problem Track your passport application Check where your application has reached using your file number and date of birth. File number 15 letters and numbers, for example DL1067123456713. It is on the acknowledgement you got at your appointment. Date of birth For example, 27 3 1990 Day Month Year Check status Your details are ready to check File number This prototype does not connect to the passport system. Continue on the official tracker and enter the same details to see your live status. Continue to the official tracker {{icon:arrow-right:22}} Check a different application What your status means Application submitted Your documents, photo and fingerprints were accepted at your appointment. Police verification in progress Your local police station is checking your details. They may visit you or ask you to visit them. Police verification report received The report has reached the Passport Office and is being reviewed. Passport granted Your application has been approved and sent for printing. Passport printed Your passport has been printed and is being prepared for posting. Passport dispatched Your passport has been sent by Speed Post. The status shows a tracking number you can use on the India Post website. If your application is on hold The Passport Office needs something from you, usually a document. Check your SMS and email, and bring what is asked for to the Passport Seva Kendra as soon as you can. If your police report is adverse Contact your Passport Office to find out why. If it can be resolved, you can ask for police verification to be done again. If you have waited a long time Call the National Call Centre on 1800-258-1800 , or register a grievance{{ext}} . Other ways to track mPassport Seva app{{ext}} Call 1800-258-1800 Related content How police verification works Apply for a passport or renew one"}];
